40 kJ heat is released for 2.4 g of C
For 1 mole 'C' :
$$\begin{array}{l}
\mathrm{Q}=\frac{40}{2.4} \times 12 \\
=\frac{400}{24} \times 12=200 \mathrm{~kJ} / \mathrm{mole}
\end{array}$$
$$\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{Q}= & \Delta \mathrm{E}=\Delta \mathrm{H}=200 \mathrm{~kJ}\left(\because \Delta \mathrm{n}_{\mathrm{g}}=0\right) \\
& \quad x=200
\end{aligned}$$
